==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|recompence||obsolete}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛkəmˌpɛns/|a=RP,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-recompense.ogg|a=Southern California}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛns|s=3}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|recompense}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|recompense}} or {{der|en|la-med|recompensa}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# An equivalent returned for anything given, done, or suffered; [[compensation]]; [[reward]]; amends; requital.
#: {{syn|en|meed|payback|recompence}}
# That which [[compensates]] for an injury, or other type of harm or damage.
#: {{syn|en|amends|recompence|remuneration|restitution|satisfaction|Thesaurus:compensation}}
#: {{ux|en|He offered money as '''recompense''' for the damage, but what the injured party wanted was an apology.}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|compensate}}
* {{l|en|recompensate}}

